            "body": "This is blocked on `pre-run-check`, which gates CI until an author has 4 merged PRs. #51627 merged yesterday so the count is 1, and this cannot run its tests until someone starts them.\n\nCould a maintainer run `/ci run`? The defect is reproducible in a few lines:\n\n```\ncommon_broadcastable_dtype([float16, bfloat16]) -> torch.float16\ncommon_broadcastable_dtype([bfloat16, float16]) -> torch.bfloat16\n```\n\nNeither is a lossless target for the other, so the function returns a dtype that violates its own docstring, and which of the two you get depends on iteration order. The cause is that `max(dtypes, key=...)` is an argmax over the input set, so it can only return a dtype that was passed in, while the correct answer here is float32. The fix is `functools.reduce(torch.promote_types, dtypes)`, and I verified it matches current behaviour on all four existing parametrised cases before adding the new one.",
            "createdAt": "2026-08-11T16:46:16Z",
            "databaseId": 5256118274,
            "updatedAt": "2026-08-11T16:46:16Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/51626#issuecomment-5256118274"
          },
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "UgaTheDev"
            },
            "body": "Rebased onto main and resolved conflict-free — this fixes `common_broadcastable_dtype` to use `torch.promote_types` instead of an argmax over the inputs, so `{float16, bfloat16}` now correctly resolves to `float32` instead of an order-dependent lossy pick. Could a maintainer take a look?",
